--
-- What this fixture discriminates: the copula/invoke split, and the fact
-- that SPACING IS NOT THE DECIDER. grammar.md R1 is ("IS never takes an
-- argument group; INVOKE always does"); CLAUDE.md §0d's spaced-vs-tight
-- rule is a canonical-layout corollary. Line 3 separates them: `count:u32`
-- is TIGHT and has no call group, so R1 says copula and spacing says
-- invoke. A scanner that highlights line 3 purple has failed H-1.
--
-- `total`, `count`, `n`, `lx`, `number` are ordinary bindings. H-4's blue
-- space is "numbers, .cases, literals, registers" and names no hue for a
-- binding, so they are `name` — UNHUED, and they do not count toward
-- coverage. See docs/spec/roles.md §3. -- gap[071]
